  "title": "VLMs: Evaluating Danger and Anomaly in Safety Reasoning",
  "summary": "This report introduces an explicit distinction between hazard and anomaly in evaluating VLMs for safety reasoning, addressing the limitations of binary safety judgments. It explores how VLMs misinterpret anomalous states as hazardous, revealing over-reliance on contextual irregularity as a proxy for danger and highlights the importance of separating anomaly from hazard for more accurate safety reasoning.",
